# The pack's Gradle build. What ships is the archives it produces -- lib/designer.apk,
# lib/sdkmanager.apk and lib/vdevice.apk, built before packing, see README -- not the toolchain that
# builds them, the jars they compile against, or Gradle's working state.
#
# The Gradle root is the repository root, so this is a list rather than one directory: `native/`
# holds only the three module directories, and everything that builds them sits beside it.
#
# Leading `/` anchors an entry to the package root. It matters here: an unanchored `gradle` matches
# by base name at any depth and takes `languages/gradle/` with it, which ships a language pack short
# of a language and says nothing about it.
native
build-libs
/gradle
/build
/.gradle
/.kotlin
gradlew
gradlew.bat
gradle.properties
settings.gradle.kts
build.gradle.kts
